      <message trigger="true" from="human" trust="principal" author="Ariel" author-id="user_01KFq3mgDbJgesJHQomDhi72" id="cmsg_01NLfVm5WfzHBRRyA4oMF5jhUy5tShbfL9cZFcQ9ACvPzi" sent-at="2026-09-27T17:12:37Z" surface="app" mention="true">No no, this skill is not for NoR finding - it&#39;s for working on a image processing algorithms. It should be helpful the next time we do some image processing. 
Skill for the development/reasearch work, with guidance on how to build the cycle:

* Getting inputs, fetching, storing, loading, caching. Large images handling.
* Creating the human-verifyable output format, probably visually with a mask on top on the input (we assume user knows what they what the output to be). This output format should be the goal/output of a human-feedback cycle. Creating the format is done on one sample input.
* Creating ground truth, as a training set, to allow a non-human-feedback cycle: a human will verify the (human verifyable) outputs on a few input images, and this would be the ground truth that the code should create the algorthms for. They would either provided by user, or if those don&#39;t exist - created by running a smart model on an input image with the requiremetns, and having a human fine-tune the results (hopefully this is beneficial. If no LLM can create a good ground-truth set - a human needs to do it manually as a prerequisite to having the self-improvment cycles)
* Essentially we’re describing an external human-feedback loop, an internal self-imrpovement-loop, and within it (a specific idea you raised) you do the build-until-working loop.
* The acceptable assumptions (based on research material, real data, and statistical inference from the images) vs. illegitimate (specific pixel counts in algorithm). Whenever we’re stuck we can perhaps look at research for specific characteristics of the thing we’re analyzing.
* In order to keep the cycles efficient - we should perform performance optimizations periodically to the WIP algorithm - the feedback cycle needs to be short and cheap (in time, token, cpu, ram), and that it handled independently from the quality improvementst (which come first).


Add this skill in the repo&#39;s local pack.</message>
