24	//      the only measure of shrink-only there is: the task's auto-merge policy
25	//      scopes a prune to the local-pack tree and judges nothing about its shape.
26	//
27	//      A commit message saying "dedup" is not enough on its own — a change that
28	//      FIXES the dedup routine says "dedup" too, and it edits the canon while
29	//      touching a local pack, which reads as a corrupt prune. So the shrink
30	//      invariant also requires the branch to be CONFINED to the local-pack
31	//      surface, which a real run always is: the routine's own first prohibition
32	//      is that it never edits the canon it prunes against. A branch reaching
33	//      outside local packs is canon work that merely mentions dedup.
